message.content:
Update the main widget block for the Zip Code Checker app at /Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Shopify App/Zip-Code.

## Step 1: Read the full liquid file first
Read `extensions/zip-code-widget/blocks/zip-code-checker.liquid` COMPLETELY (504 lines). Understand:
- Where DEFAULTS object is (around lines 101-123)
- Where `checkZip()` function is and exactly what happens after `data.allowed` check
- Where button click/enter key handlers are (around lines 211-301)
- The `inp` variable (the ZIP input field)
- The `btn` variable (the Check button)
- The `res` variable (result container)
- CSS section location
- Where waitlist rendering happens

---

## Change 1: ZIP Code Format Normalization

Add a `normalizeZip` helper function BEFORE the `checkZip` function:

```javascript
function normalizeZip(raw) {
  var z = raw.trim().toUpperCase();
  z = z.replace(/\s+/g, '');        // collapse all spaces (UK: SW1A 2AA → SW1A2AA)
  z = z.replace(/-\d{4}$/, '');     // strip US ZIP+4 suffix (90210-1234 → 90210)
  return z;
}
```

In `checkZip()`, change the first line from:
```javascript
var zip = inp.value.trim();
```
to:
```javascript
var zip = normalizeZip(inp.value);
inp.value = zip;  // Update the input field to show the normalized value (clean UX)
```

---

## Change 2: sessionStorage Bridge + Add to Cart Blocking

In the DEFAULTS object, add these new config keys (they'll be populated from the merchant's saved config):
```javascript
blockCartOnInvalid: false,
showSocialProof: true,
```

After the `checkZip()` `then(data => {` block resolves, add sessionStorage writes. Find the exact location where success and failure are handled, and add:

**At the TOP of the `.then(data => { ... })` handler (before the if/else):**
```javascript
// Store validation result for cart page
try {
  sessionStorage.setItem('zcc:valid', data.allowed ? 'true' : 'false');
  sessionStorage.setItem('zcc:zip', zip);
  sessionStorage.setItem('zcc:shop', SHOP);
  // Fire custom event for other scripts to listen to
  window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('zcc:validated', {
    detail: { valid: data.allowed, zip: zip }
  }));
} catch(e) { /* sessionStorage may be unavailable */ }
```

**After showing the success/failure result (at the END of `.then(data => { ... })` but inside it):**
```javascript
// Block/unblock Add to Cart based on result (if merchant enabled this)
if (cfg.blockCartOnInvalid) {
  var ATC_SELECTORS = [
    'button[name="add"]',
    '.product-form__submit',
    '[data-product-add]',
    '.btn--add-to-cart',
    '.product-form button[type="submit"]',
    'button.shopify-payment-button__button',
    '.shopify-payment-button button',
    'button.product-form__cart-submit'
  ].join(',');

  try {
    var atcBtns = document.querySelectorAll(ATC_SELECTORS);
    atcBtns.forEach(function(b) {
      if (!b.closest('#zcc-widget, [data-zcc-widget]')) { // Don't touch our own widget's button
        if (data.allowed) {
          b.disabled = false;
          b.style.opacity = '';
          b.title = b.getAttribute('data-zcc-orig-title') || '';
          b.removeAttribute('data-zcc-orig-title');
          b.removeAttribute('data-zcc-blocked');
        } else {
          b.setAttribute('data-zcc-orig-title', b.title || '');
          b.disabled = true;
          b.style.opacity = '0.5';
          b.title = 'Please enter a valid ZIP code to continue';
          b.setAttribute('data-zcc-blocked', 'true');
        }
      }
    });
  } catch(e) { /* DOM query may fail in some contexts */ }
}
```

**Add to the `.catch()` handler (network errors):**
```javascript
try {
  sessionStorage.setItem('zcc:valid', 'false');
  window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('zcc:validated', { detail: { valid: false, zip: zip } }));
} catch(e) {}
```

**Also restore buttons when the ZIP input is cleared.** Find where the input event listener is (if it exists) or add one. After the button click event listener, add:
```javascript
// Re-enable buttons when customer clears the input
inp.addEventListener('input', function() {
  if (!inp.value.trim() && cfg.blockCartOnInvalid) {
    try {
      var blocked = document.querySelectorAll('[data-zcc-blocked="true"]');
      blocked.forEach(function(b) {
        b.disabled = false;
        b.style.opacity = '';
        b.title = b.getAttribute('data-zcc-orig-title') || '';
        b.removeAttribute('data-zcc-blocked');
        b.removeAttribute('data-zcc-orig-title');
      });
      sessionStorage.removeItem('zcc:valid');
      sessionStorage.removeItem('zcc:zip');
    } catch(e) {}
  }
});
```

---

## Change 3: Social Proof on Waitlist Form

Find the waitlist rendering section — where the email input and "Join Waitlist" button are shown after a blocked result.

BEFORE the email input in the waitlist form, add social proof text:
```javascript
// Social proof count
if (cfg.showSocialProof && data.waitlistCount && data.waitlistCount > 0) {
  var spEl = document.createElement('div');
  spEl.className = 'zcc-social-proof';
  var count = data.waitlistCount;
  spEl.textContent = '\uD83D\uDE4B Join ' + count + ' other' + (count !== 1 ? 's' : '') + ' waiting for delivery to your area';
  wlSection.appendChild(spEl);
}
```

Note: `wlSection` is whatever variable holds the waitlist container. Read the file to find the exact variable name used for the waitlist section element — it might be `wl`, `wlDiv`, `waitlistEl`, etc. Use the correct variable name from the existing code.

---

## Change 4: Add CSS for new classes

Find the CSS `<style>` section. Add:
```css
.zcc-social-proof { 
  display: block; 
  font-size: 0.82em; 
  color: #6d7175; 
  margin-bottom: 8px; 
  font-style: italic;
}
```

---

## Change 5: Add wrapper ID to widget container

On the main widget container div (the outermost div rendered in all 3 modes — inline, floating, popup), add `id="zcc-widget"` so the ATC blocking logic can exclude our own button from being disabled. Read the file to find the correct place.

---

## Important Notes:
- Read the FULL file before making ANY changes
- Preserve ALL existing functionality — do not break success states, blocked states, floating/popup modes
- Match existing JavaScript style exactly (var/function declarations, not let/const/arrow functions)
- The liquid file may be large (504 lines) — be careful about line numbers when editing
- Test your changes mentally: inline mode, floating mode, popup mode should all still work

## DO NOT run typecheck (this is a .liquid file, not TypeScript)

